# Copy to `.env.local` to point the demo at a server.
#
# With none of these set the demo runs single player: the plugin installs its
# offline adapter, every system runs its normal code path, and nothing is sent.

# Phoenix socket endpoint. Setting this is what turns multiplayer on.
# Start the server first: cd ../demo_server && mix deps.get && mix phx.server
# VITE_PHOENIX_ENDPOINT=ws://localhost:4000/socket

# Room to join. The Phoenix topic is `room:<value>`.
# VITE_PHOENIX_ROOM=lobby

# `host_relayed` (default) forwards frames untouched.
# `server_authoritative` re-simulates input on the server and enables client
# prediction with reconciliation.
# VITE_PHOENIX_MODE=host_relayed

# Metres/second used by client prediction. Must match the server's
# `:move_speed`, or every step you take is corrected.
# VITE_PHOENIX_MOVE_SPEED=4.5
